@startuml
title Solving one region (1024x1024 blocks, 16x16 macro-cells)

start
:Chunk request lands in\nan unsolved region;
:Check all 4 neighbor directions\nfor an already-cached region\n(never force-solve one that's missing);
:Fix that/those cached edge(s)\nas boundary constraints;\nunconstrained on any side\nwith no cached neighbor yet;
:Place seeds inside region\n(blue-noise, deterministic\nfrom world seed + region coords,\nspaced per target biome size);

repeat
  :Grow each seed outward\nacross macro-cells\n(flood-fill toward size target);
  if (growth hits adjacency\nviolation with a neighbor region/seed?) then (yes)
    if (another candidate biome fits\nsize class + all touched neighbors?) then (yes)
      :Reassign seed to\nnext candidate biome;
    else (no)
      if (backtrack depth cap reached?) then (yes)
        :Log warning\n(graph-config bug signal);
        :Assign universal-filler\nbiome to this seed;
      else (no)
        :Backtrack to previous\nseed decision, try its\nnext candidate;
      endif
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
repeat while (any region still\nbelow its target size range\nand growable?) is (yes)
->no;

note right
  Never relax a constraint.
  Universal-filler biome node
  guarantees a legal candidate
  always exists eventually.
end note

:Gap-fill pass: assign any\nunclaimed cell the most common\nlegal neighboring biome,\nor universal filler if none;
:Write macro-cell -> biome-id\nfor this region to cache;
stop
@enduml
